~ core.time — time primitives. `@sleep` is a leaf IO primitive (the `@` marker), reached
~ through the `time` binding as `time.@sleep(seconds)`; `now` is a plain clock read,
~ reached as `time.now()`.
~ Import with `<< core.time`.

~ Pause the current fiber for `seconds` seconds (a fractional Num), then continue.
>> @sleep = (seconds :: Num) -> $ => < $ >

~ Seconds on a monotonic clock (a fractional Num), called `time.now()`. Only DIFFERENCES
~ between two readings are meaningful, which is what measures elapsed time.
>> now = () -> Num => < 0 >
